<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<job id="recruitment-eve-brief" xmlns="http://xmlns.jcp.org/xml/ns/javaee" version="1.0">
    <!--
    Recruitment Eve Brief Job (V531)

    Purpose:
    One Slack DM per interviewer the WORKING DAY BEFORE their interviews:
    candidate, position, round (or informal chat), day, time and place,
    the template's focus areas, the kit deep link and - when
    recruitment.slack.scorecard.enabled is on - a "Fill in scorecard"
    button per round. No interviews in the window means no message.

    Why it exists:
    The 06:00 day-of brief (recruitment-morning-brief.xml) cannot do this
    job. For a 09:00 interview it lands three hours before the room, which
    is too late to read a CV or move anything. This brief goes out
    mid-afternoon the working day before, while there is still a day left
    to act on it. The day-of brief is kept and degrades to a short
    schedule line for any pair this one already covered.

    Working-day-before:
    recruitment.brief.lead-days days back from the interview date, then
    backwards off Saturday and Sunday. A Monday interview therefore
    briefs on Friday, and Friday's run covers Saturday, Sunday and Monday
    in a single DM. A run on a weekend sends nothing.

    Every briefed (interviewer, interview) pair appends its own
    EVE_BRIEF_SENT event carrying brief_date - the date the brief COVERS,
    not the date it was sent - so the run only briefs pairs with no event
    for that interview's date, and re-runs and concurrent instances (ECS
    cutover) never double-DM. A reschedule onto a different date re-arms
    the brief by construction, because the stored brief_date no longer
    matches. Only interviews in SCHEDULED state at run time brief. All
    side effects are gated by recruitment.pipeline.enabled AND
    recruitment.slack.eve-brief.enabled (off = no-op).

    Schedule:
    Daily at 13:00 UTC via BatchScheduler (15:00 Copenhagen in summer,
    14:00 in winter), gated by
    dk.trustworks.recruitment.eve-brief.enabled (default true).

    Similar to:
    recruitment-morning-brief.xml (the P23 day-of sibling, same service)
    -->

    <listeners>
        <listener ref="jobMonitoringListener"/>
    </listeners>

    <step id="send-recruitment-eve-briefs">
        <listeners>
            <listener ref="stepProgressListener"/>
        </listeners>

        <batchlet ref="recruitmentEveBriefBatchlet"/>
    </step>
</job>
